PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • Data: useCostBreakdown (GET /analytics/tco?vehicle_id=) -> CostBreakdownData {monthly_breakdown[{month,ev_cost}],
    total_charging_cost, total_savings, monthly_savings, cost_per_km_ev}; useVehicles resolves the active vehicle id
    in the source seam; useFormatting/useUnits supply currencySymbol/precision/distance via the snapshot prefs.
  • Donut: web Recharts PieChart (innerRadius 55%, outerRadius 85%, paddingAngle 2) over the LAST 6 months ->
    Swift Charts SectorMark(innerRadius .ratio(0.55), angularInset 2, cornerRadius 3); slice fills from
    TSChartPalette.color(at:) (= web useThemeChartPalette().series, modulo-wrapped). The web hover CostTooltip
    (slice month + formatCurrency(value, 2)) becomes a touch-first center read-out (default = most-recent month,
    tap focuses a slice) per Apple HIG — no hover on touch.
  • Ranked list: web WidgetRankedList sorts descending and caps at 5; the projector reproduces this (stable ties).
    The web `barColor` is a hex string applied as a Tailwind className (a latent no-op, so the web bars render
    colorless); the native row renders the INTENDED value bar tinted with the same palette colour at 0.15 opacity
    (web `opacity-15`). This is an intent-faithful enhancement of a latent web bug, documented here (no silent drift).
  • Cost / {unit}: cost_per_km_ev passes through for km and scales by MI_TO_KM (1.60934) for mi, pinned to
    $0.050 (km) / $0.080 (mi) by executed assertions; zero -> em dash. Gas Savings -> $value (+"Lifetime") or em dash.
  • Compact (cols<=1): WidgetBigNumber = fmtNumber(currentMonthCost, 0) + trailing currencySymbol, "This Month"
    label, "Saved {amount} vs gas" subtitle (monthly_savings>0), "Saving" success badge (total_savings>0).
  • States: loading (skeleton), empty (ContentUnavailableView), error (retry), stale (chip + auto-refresh),
    offline (cached + banner), content. Reduce Motion + Dynamic Type (minimumScaleFactor) honored.

